# CODEOWNERS (Issue 13): who reviews what. GitHub requests a review from the owner of every path a
# pull request touches, and the "main: review" ruleset requires that owner's approval.
#
# Encoded from docs/TEAM/WORKLOAD_SPLIT.md §2, translated to this repository's layout (§2 was
# written for an `app/` package; the code lives in `src/`). Every path has exactly one owner. Where
# §2 names two roles, the first owns the path and the second is its backup reviewer.
#
# Roles and handles (WORKLOAD_SPLIT §1). Until the team fills in §1, every role routes to the
# DevOps/QA Lead, who reassigns the review. To hand a role over, replace its handle on the lines
# tagged with that role; tests/unit/platform/test_team_workflow.py checks every owner is in §1.
#
#   Role                      Handle        Backup reviewer (§1)
#   A  Backend Lead           @Billykat7    B
#   B  Backend/Integrations   @Billykat7    A
#   C  Frontend/Patient       @Billykat7    D
#   D  Frontend/Clinic        @Billykat7    C
#   E  DevOps/QA Lead         @Billykat7    F
#   F  Data & Research        @Billykat7    E
#
# Review SLA: 24 hours on a weekday; after that the backup reviewer may approve (CONTRIBUTING.md).
# The last matching line wins, so the catch-all comes first and the most specific paths last.
# Comments sit on their own lines: CODEOWNERS has no trailing comments.

